meta-secureedge-distro
=====================

Distribution configuration for Yocto Project Scarthgap.

The secureedge distribution inherits Poky's distribution configuration and sets
the SecureEdge name, version and SDK vendor. It selects systemd and usrmerge and
removes sysvinit. Image contents and service hardening belong to the platform
layer and selected image, not the distribution name alone.

Dependencies and integration
----------------------------

The layer declares core and its distribution configuration requires Poky. Kas
profiles select distro: secureedge with meta-secureedge-platform. Raspberry Pi
uses raspberrypi0-2w-64; QEMU uses qemuarm64.

See docs/build.md at the repository root for pinned profile dependencies
and container prerequisites. A distribution or
machine selection alone is not evidence of a successful build.

License and provenance
----------------------

COPYING.MIT is preserved unchanged. The root LICENSE grants MIT licensing for
original SecureEdge-owned source, scripts, tests, configuration and documentation,
subject to third-party exceptions described in the root README.md Licensing
section. External components retain their own licenses. The 16 original platform recipes
previously declaring CLOSED now declare MIT and checksum Yocto's common MIT text;
third-party and firmware redistribution obligations remain separate.
